      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T22:08:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, we constantly change the way Gerrit works, including notifications.\nIf any change in behavior is a _breaking change_, then this will be the only section with a list of items, apart from the pure bug fixes.\n\nThe purpose of this section is to notify the Gerrit admin that any existing end-to-end functionality will break if they upgrade, and they\u0027ll need to change something (config, rules, scripts, other apps) to make it work again.\n\nExample 1: I am calling a REST API/foo with parameter bar\u003d1, but in v3.15, if I make the same call, it returns a 400, and I need to change it by amending the parameter to bar\u003d2.\n\nExample 2: I am calling the `gerrit show-caches` SSH command and parsing the output ... but the output doesn\u0027t include the stats anymore, and my script would fail. I read the release notes, and I understand that by adding `include-diskstats\u003dtrue,` I can adapt my scripting and still fetch the statistics as I was doing before.",
      "parentUuid": "d7d4bdd9_a6b19eb2",
